 new run without the field.",rR="task_id of the subagent (local_agent) task whose agent launched this subagent, shell, monitor or workflow task. Absent when the launcher is the main thread, has no task_id of its own (a teammate, an agent inside a workflow), or is no longer tracked. A resumed subagent keeps its original parent. The parent may be a foreground or already-ended task, so treat an unknown id as no parent.",Qt="Id of one run of the task: equal on every task_* event, background_tasks_changed entry and saved notification (its origin.runId) of that run. A resumed task keeps its task_id and gets a new one. The run ids of one task sort, by plain string comparison, in the order the runs opened; a frame that names a run sorting before the one a reader shows is late. Nothing else about the format is promised. Absent for a task this process did not register, and from CLIs that predate it.",AW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("task_notification"),task_id:o(),run_id:o().optional().describe(Qt),tool_use_id:o().optional(),status:B(["completed","failed","stopped"]),reason:B(["worker_restart"]).optional().describe("Machine-readable cause, set only when the task did not end through an ordinary completion, failure, or stop. 'worker_restart': the worker process restarted and the resumed process found the task orphaned (always with status 'stopped')."),output_file:o(),summary:o(),usage:u({total_tokens:E().int(),tool_uses:E().int(),duration_ms:E().int()}).optional(),resource_links:C(VA()).optional().describe("CLI-owned: for a backgrounded MCP task (task_type mcp_task) that completed, the `resource_link` content blocks of its final result \u2014 the files it returned by reference \u2014 collected from the raw result before the CLI renders it as the text the model reads. A backgrounded task's tool_result is the placeholder text and its real result arrives as this notification, so this is where a host learns which files that tool call produced; join to the originating call via tool_use_id. Same fields and caps as tool_use_result.resourceLinks (at most 50 links, 64 KiB serialized), absent when the result had none or the task is any other type. Never populated from the server's _meta."),handback:B(gXr).optional().describe("@internal Present on a 'completed' notification of a subagent that reports through the SubagentHandback tool: how its report reached its caller, with the values and meaning of `handback` on AgentToolCompletedOutput. Left out when the subagent failed, was stopped, is waiting on agents it started, or is waiting on its own background work with nothing delivered yet; for such a subagent, `summary` is then not a report. When present, `summary` holds harness notes written for the model. Any notification can be followed by a later one for the same task_id when the agent is resumed or finishes its wait; the later one replaces what the earlier one showed."),handback_report:hXr().optional().describe("@internal The report a 'send' or 'flagged' hand-back delivered, the same shape as `handbackReport` on AgentToolCompletedOutput: when present, render it instead of `summary`, with its `warning`, if it has one, above its `text`. Absent for 'withheld'; if it is absent for another value too, show `summary`."),skip_transcript:M().optional(),ambient:M().optional().describe(Ao),uuid:p(),session_id:o()})),RW=f(()=>u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("task_started"),task_id:o(),run_id:o().optional().describe(Qt),tool_use_id:o().optional(),description:o(),subagent_type:o().optional().describe("Subagent type for Task tool subagents."),is_backgrounded:M().optional().describe("Whether the task was registered in the background (true) or in the foreground with the spawning tool call blocking on it (false). A resumed subagent is always registered in the background. A later move to the background arrives as task_updated patch.is_backgrounded. Set for local_agent and local_bash tasks."),awaited:M().optional().describe(nR),spawn_depth:E().int().optional().de