r restricted; it keeps its stats. Such rows include: a binary or untracked file; a symlink in the base commit; a submodule; a file under a git filter or working-tree-encoding; an index entry marked skip-worktree or assume-unchanged whose file on disk is not what the entry holds; and a file whose path on disk cannot be proven to be the one git listed, which is one reached through a link or junction, or, on a volume blind to letter case or Unicode form (macOS and Windows by default), one whose name or folder is spelled otherwise on disk than in git's index."),skippedLarge:C(o()).describe("Paths whose diff text exceeded the per-file or aggregate size cap, so they have stats but no hunks."),restricted:C(o()).describe("Paths whose hunk content was withheld by the diff surface's content-provenance gate: read-permission rules (same gate as read_file) plus this surface's stricter file-identity checks (symlink and hardlinked worktree files are refused here even where read_file serves them; so is a path that git diff lists as changed but that git holds in neither the diff's base commit nor the index). Stats remain visible."),source:Fe([u({kind:T("working-tree")}),u({kind:T("branch"),baseBranch:o(),baseRef:o()})])}).nullable()}).describe("@internal Workspace git diff for the thin-client /diff dialog. diff is null when the workspace is not a git repo or is in a transient git state (merge/rebase/cherry-pick). Paths in skippedLarge carry no hunks entry at all \u2014 membership alone marks them as too large. An entirely empty hunks array with non-empty perFileStats is not by itself a failure signal: it is the normal shape when all changes are untracked (stats only \u2014 git diff emits no hunks for untracked files) or every file was withheld, and can also occur when the hunks fetch transiently failed and only stats are available.")),ca=f(()=>u({subtype:T("get_plan")}).describe("@internal Read the session's current plan-mode plan. Unlike read_file, the caller does not need to know 