ne it could present; those are named in ignored_tools). Absent from a worker that does not adopt them (an older one, or one with adoption switched off) and while the worker cannot read the organisation's policy yet (passthrough_declined 'pending'); then the worker has taken none of these tools, and a machine connected to the device bridge keeps serving its MCP tools over it. Also absent from the reply to an announce marked 'still_here', and to one marked 'sleeping' when the worker reads that mark (any other worker answers it as an ordinary announce); such an announce changes nothing the worker took before."),passthrough_declined:B(["policy","pending","unavailable"]).optional().describe("@internal Why the worker adopted none of the machine's MCP tools this announce carried. 'policy': the organisation's MCP server policy blocks the device bridge's server (or, in a session without one, an address it could have), the session is in safe mode, or the session has no such server and the worker cannot work out the address that server would have (for example, outside a CCR session); passthrough_adopted is 0, and the machine need not re-announce those tools. 'pending': the organisation's managed settings are still loading, so the tools wait for the machine's next announce; passthrough_adopted is absent, and a machine connected to the device bridge keeps serving its MCP tools over it meanwhile. 'unavailable': sent only by older workers, which adopted none when the session had no server for the device bridge; passthrough_adopted is 0, and the machine need not re-announce those tools. Absent otherwise."),ignored_tools:C(o()).optional().describe("@internal Announced entries the worker did not adopt, at most 32 named: an unknown native name, a malformed or duplicate entry, or an MCP tool beyond the most it keeps, whose name it could not present as announced, whose name the session service keeps for itself, or whose input schema the API cannot take."),worker_capabilities:C(o()).max(