sage is applied the way --model is at start-up: it writes no /model entries to the transcript and makes no extra API call to confirm a model id the local checks accept. Accepted once, only on a parked spare, only before any turn. A request that fails validation is refused before anything is touched and leaves the spare parked; a failure after that point leaves the spare unusable (discard it).")),c1=f(()=>u({status:T("ok"),cwd:o().optional().describe("Canonical working directory the session now runs in (omitted when the canonical path carries invisible or non-printing characters, which are never echoed)."),session_id:o(),parked_ms:E().optional().describe("How long the spare was parked before this claim."),sdk_mcp_settled:M().describe("Whether the in-process SDK MCP handshakes registered while parked had completed when the claim arrived (false: the first turn still waits for them)."),initialize:me(o(),oe()).optional().describe("Present when include_initialize was true: the initialize-shaped payload for the claimed session."),workspace_trust_recorded:M().optional().describe("As initialize's workspace_trust_recorded: present when the claim came from the process that owns the CLI's stdin and carried workspace_trust with accepted true and an absolute directory; true when the claimed folder is now recorded as trusted (or already was), false when the attestation was not honored.")}).describe("@internal Result of a successful claim_session. Failures arrive as a control_response error whose message starts with a reason token (not_a_spare, already_claimed, busy, turn_started, env_key_not_claimable:<KEY>, cwd_not_found, cwd_not_a_directory, \u2026); the spare stays parked after any of them.")),Aa=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_reconnect"),serverName:o()}).describe("Reconnects a disconnected or failed MCP server.")),Ra=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_toggle"),serverName:o(),enabled:M()}).describe("Enables or disables an MCP server.")),va=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_read_resource"),serverName:o().d