- If you read a file that exists but has empty contents you will receive a system reminder warning in place of file contents.${nr}`}function fl(){return`
- If this is an existing file, you MUST use the ${qe} tool first to read the file's contents. This tool will fail if you did not read the file first.`}function qni(e,n){if(RM({model:e,leanPrompt:n}))return`Writes a file to the local filesystem, overwriting if one exists.

When to use: creating a new file, or fully replacing one you've already ${qe}. Overwriting an existing file you haven't ${qe} will fail. For partial changes, use ${at} instead.`;return`Writes a file to the local filesystem.

