n.consent_forced_off":"This computer's settings turn off unattended commands from cloud sessions (remoteTools.allowUnattendedServing).","auto_off.reason.settings":"This computer's settings turn auto mode off (disableAutoMode).","auto_off.reason.breaker":"Auto mode is turned off for the Claude Code process running on this computer. Restarting it checks again.",auto_off_notice(e,n){return`Auto mode is off for ${e}: you are asked to approve what your cloud session runs there. ${n}`},"ask.outside_sandbox":"Runs outside the sandbox.","ask.settings_person_only":"This may change Claude Code's settings or credentials, so only you can approve it.",ask_runs_in_vm(e){return`This runs in a ${e} VM on this computer, not on the computer itself.`},"serving_off.muted":"Remote tool serving was turned off by Anthropic (emergency switch). No new command is accepted until it is turned back on. A command Claude is waiting on may go on until the cloud session cancels it.","serving_on.unmuted":"Remote tool serving was turned back on by Anthropic. Commands can run on this computer again.","serving_off.profile_dirs_unreadable":"This computer's tools are not offered to your cloud session: Windows did not say where your profile folders are (AppData, the Start Menu, and Documents, where your PowerShell profile lives). Restarting Claude Code tries again; the debug log says why.","serving_off.mount_table_unreadable":"This computer's tools are not offered to your cloud session: the list of mounted drives (/proc/self/mountinfo) could not be read in full. It is read again every few minutes; if this lasts, see the debug log.","serving_off.bridge_trusted_devices":"This computer's tools are not offered to your cloud session over the device bridge. The bridge cannot check a device's proof, and trusted devices may be required for your organization or could not be checked. Remove the off switch for the session channel from your environment to serve over it instead.","serving_off.vm_starting":"Your cloud session's calls wait on this computer for now: the VM they must run in is still starting. They run as soon as it is ready.","serving_off.vm_unavailable":"Your cloud session's calls are refused on this computer: it is set to run them only inside a VM, and the VM is not available.","call_refused.settings_unreadable":"A call from your cloud session was refused: this computer could not read all of its settings, so it could not tell whether tools must run inside a VM. Its tools are still offered, and the next call is judged afresh. Check that your settings files are valid and that your organization's settings have loaded.","served_settings.folder_config_not_used":"This folder's hooks and plugin settings are not used while this computer serves a cloud session. The session may have written them: review them first; put only your own in ~/.claude/settings.json.","served_settings.changed_while_attached":"This project's Claude Code settings changed while a cloud session was using this computer, so the change waits. Run claude apply-project-settings in a terminal in this folder to review. Cloud sessions keep using what you accepted. The cloud session may have made the change.","served_settings.held_back":"This project's Claude Code settings differ from what you accepted for cloud sessions, which keep using what you accepted. Run claude apply-project-settings in a terminal in this folder to review. A cloud session may have made the change.","served_settings.own_waiting":"Run claude apply-project-settings in a terminal: cloud sessions are not using your own Claude Code settings as they stand, and a change in them waits for you.","served_settings.own_waiting.session_note":"The person's own Claude Code settings on this computer hold something they have not accepted for cloud sessions, so allow rules in them may not count here and a command may be asked about. Tell the user: to review, run claude apply-project-settings in a terminal on this computer.","served_settings.taken_as_found":"A cloud session used this computer before: check .claude/settings.json and settings.local.json. Cloud sessions use them as they are; later changes wait until you run claude apply-project-settings.","served_settings.record_unavailable":"Cloud sessions cannot use this computer until it can read and save its record of this folder's Claude Code settings. Check free disk space and that ~/.claude/state can be written, then reconnect it.","served_settings.project_env_not_applied":"This project's Claude Code settings set environment variables not applied while this computer serves a cloud session. The session may have set them; put only your own in ~/.claude/settings.json here.","refused.sandbox_custody":"This computer can't run this command inside its sandbox while protecting its credential files (a protected directory could not be prepared). Nothing was run. Ask the user to run it themselves on this computer, or continue without it.","refused.path_too_long"(e,n){return`${e} cannot open this path: written out in full it comes to ${n.toLocaleString("en-US")} bytes or more, and its operating system takes no path that long. Nothing was read or written.`},"computer_folder.prompt.name":"Use a folder on your computer","computer_folder.prompt.question":"Let this cloud session use a folder on your computer?","computer_folder.prompt.meaning":"Claude in this cloud session can then run commands and read and change files in that folder, including in auto mode, under that computer\u2019s own sandbox, rules and hooks. To end it, stop claude remote-control on that computer or disconnect it in the Claude app.","computer_folder.prompt.folder"(e){return`folder: ${e}`},"computer_folder.prompt.computer"(e){return`on: ${e}`},"repository_trust.state.trusted":"Repositories trusted","repository_trust.state.no_repository":"No repository attached","repository_trust.state.declined":"Repository trust declined","repository_trust.state.not_marked":"Repositories not marked trusted","repository_trust.prompt.meaning":"Answering yes marks everything attached to this cloud session as trusted, which lets the session act on your computer with your authority. Say yes only if you trust all of it.","repository_trust.prompt.unbound":"This terminal is not the computer this cloud session is bound to, so an answer given here cannot prove which device it came from. Answer on a device that can: claude.ai on the web, the desktop app or the mobile app.","repository_trust.prompt.not_shown_here":"This cloud session is asking whether you trust what is attached to it, but the question cannot be shown in full here. Answer it in claude.ai on the web, the desktop app or the mobile app; the session waits until you do (esc stops its turn).","repository_trust.prompt.answer_elsewhere"(e){return`This cloud session is asking whether you trust what is attached to it. A yes given here would not count, because an answer sent from here cannot prove which device it came from. Answer on a trusted device, at ${e} or in the desktop or mobile app; the session waits until you do (esc stops its turn).`},"repository_trust.folder_waits.required":"Before this session can use a folder on your computer, it needs you to confirm you trust what is attached to it. It asks next.","repository_trust.folder_waits.declined":"This session cannot use a folder on your computer: you declined to trust what is attached to it. Send it a new message if you want it to ask again.","repository_trust.folder_waits.unavailable":"This session cannot use a folder on your computer right now: the service could not read what is attached to it. It can try again.","repository_trust.folder_waits.not_elevated":"Before this session can use a folder on your computer, it needs you to agree to limit it to your trusted devices, for good. If it can ask you, it does so next; answer in Claude on the web or in the desktop app.","repository_trust.folder_waits.marker":"(The service's own message to Claude is not shown here; the transcript view show